viders-and-runtimes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes","content":"`runtime.kind` selects the execution backend: `RuntimeKinds.CONTAINER`\r\n(the default, `\"container\"`), `RuntimeKinds.SPOT_CONTAINER`\r\n(`\"spot_container\"`), or `RuntimeKinds.LAMBDA` (`\"lambda\"`)."},"129":{"id":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes","content":"`runtime.size` selects a managed machine-size preset; use `Sizes.*` in\r\nTypeScript."},"130":{"id":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes","content":"Omit either field to use its default (`container` for `kind` and\r\n`shared-0.25x-1gb` for `size`). The CLI equivalents are `--runtime <kind>` and\r\n`--runtime-size <size>`."},"131":{"id":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/providers-and-runtimes#cli","content":"Events, files, cleanup, and downloads use the same SDK and CLI surface for\r\nevery provider. For the exact supported model list, use the generated\r\nprovider/runtime capability matrix."},"132":{"id":"/docs/concepts/sessions","page_id":"/docs/concepts/sessions","type":"page","content":"Sessions","breadcrumbs":["aex","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/sessions"},"133":{"id":"/docs/concepts/sessions-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/sessions","content":"Resumable threads, explicit runs, and committed checkpoints."},"134":{"id":"/docs/concepts/sessions-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/sessions","content":"A session is a resumable thread. Its `status` describes whether that thread can\r\nprogress, not whether the previous run succeeded. Typical resumable states are\r\n`running`, `idle`, `suspended`, `awaiting_approval`, and recoverable `error`.\r\nThe previous run verdict is available as `lastRun.outcome` and on its terminal\r\nRUN event."},"135":{"id":"/docs/concepts/sessions-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/sessions","content":"`finished()` resolves only after `RUN_FINISHED` or `RUN_ERROR`. A\r\n`RUN_FINISHED` is the consistency barrier: session state, usage, checkpoint,\r\nand checkpoint-backed files are committed before it is emitted. This release does not\r\nexpose a separate pre-checkpoint \"brain idle\" wait. The committed session\r\nprojection must identify that exact run in `lastRun`; an idle projection with a\r\nmissing or older `lastRun` is treated as inconsistent and `finished()` fails."},"136":{"id":"/docs/concepts/sessions-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/sessions","content":"The three common namespaces are stable properties:"},"137":{"id":"/docs/concepts/sessions-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/sessions","content":"Reopen a durable session with `aex.sessions.open(id)`. Use a stable\r\n`idempotencyKey` for create and message mutations that your application may\r\nrepeat. Reads and explicitly idempotent mutations receive bounded transport\r\nretries; a user run is never replayed as a whole by the SDK."},"138":{"id":"/docs/concepts/sessions-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/sessions","content":"`aex.start(...)` is the one-shot create, send, and finish convenience. It\r\nreturns the same five-value run outcome and committed file snapshot."},"139":{"id":"/docs/concepts/subagents","page_id":"/docs/concepts/subagents","type":"page","content":"Subagents","breadcrumbs":["aex","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/subagents"},"140":{"id":"/docs/concepts/subagents-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/subagents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/subagents","content":"Delegate bounded work to child sessions and inspect their lineage."},"141":{"id":"/docs/concepts/subagents-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/subagents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/subagents","content":"The builtin `subagent` capability lets an agent delegate work to child sessions.\r\nEnable it with the default builtin set or include it explicitly in\r\n`builtinTools`. Use `builtinTools: \"none\"` to disable agent-driven delegation."},"142":{"id":"/docs/concepts/subagents-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/subagents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/subagents","content":"Children are durable session records with their own events and checkpointed\r\nfiles. Discover them from the parent handle:"},"143":{"id":"/docs/concepts/subagents-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/subagents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/subagents","content":"Child `status` is a session lifecycle state. Inspect `lastRun.outcome` or the\r\nchild's terminal RUN event for its run verdict. Child handles are read-only:\r\nthey expose events, checkpointed files, and recursive lineage, but not top-level\r\nsession controls such as send, cancel, suspend, resume, or delete."},"144":{"id":"/docs/concepts/subagents-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/subagents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/subagents","content":"Provider credentials are inherited through the hosted runtime's vaulted\r\nchannel; they are not copied into public child submissions or event payloads.\r\nDepth, breadth, and spend limits are enforced server-side. Use\r\n`overrides.maxSpendUsd` and a deliberate builtin selection to bound a parent\r\nworkflow."},"145":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","type":"page","content":"Authentication","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/authentication"},"146":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/authentication#authentication","content":"Authentication"},"147":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/authentication#getting-a-token-invite-only-beta","content":"Getting a token (invite-only beta)"},"148":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/authentication#using-a-token","content":"Using a token"},"149":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/authentication#plane-routing-and-the-baseurl-guard","content":"Plane routing and the `baseUrl` guard"},"150":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Scopes"},"151":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/authentication#introspection-whoami","content":"Introspection: `whoami`"},"152":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/authentication#rotation-and-revocation","content":"Rotation and revocation"},"153":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#authentication","content":"Every SDK and CLI call authenticates with an **aex API key**: a bearer\r\ncredential that is **workspace-scoped** — the workspace is derived server-side\r\nfrom the token, so there is no workspace parameter anywhere in the API. A\r\nrequest either carries a valid token for a workspace or it is rejected with\r\n`401 unauthorized` (see Errors)."},"154":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#getting-a-token-invite-only-beta","content":"aex is currently in **invite-only beta**. Workspaces and their initial API\r\ntokens are provisioned by the aex team — contact support\\@aex.dev for beta\r\naccess. Once your workspace exists, you can create and delete additional tokens\r\nin the dashboard at https\\://aex.dev."},"155":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#using-a-token","content":"Pass the token to the SDK constructor, the CLI's `--api-key` flag, or persist\r\nit once with `aex login`:"},"156":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#using-a-token","content":"(`new Aex(apiKey)` is the canonical constructor; the equivalent options form is\r\ndocumented once in Credentials.)"},"157":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#using-a-token","content":"The token travels as a standard `Authorization: Bearer` header. Treat it like\r\nany other secret: keep it in environment variables or a secret manager, never\r\nin session config, prompts, or committed files."},"158":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#plane-routing-and-the-baseurl-guard","content":"An aex API key is **self-describing**: it embeds the plane (`dev` / `prd`) and\r\nregion it was minted for. The constructor parses the key and routes accordingly,\r\nwith **zero network**:"},"159":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#plane-routing-and-the-baseurl-guard","content":"**Omit `baseUrl`** and the key routes to its canonical hosted API plane:\r\n`prd` keys route to `https://api.aex.dev`, and `dev` keys route to\r\n`https://dev-api.aex.dev`."},"160":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#plane-routing-and-the-baseurl-guard","content":"**Supply a `baseUrl` whose plane disagrees with the key** (e.g. a `dev` key\r\npointed at `https://api.aex.dev`) and the constructor throws\r\n`CredentialValidationError` **before any request** — you no longer discover the\r\nmismatch as a late `401 token_invalid` after a full round-trip."},"161":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"A token carries a set of **scopes**; every API route requires one, and a token\r\nthat lacks the route's scope fails with `403 insufficient_scope` naming the\r\nmissing scope. The customer-grantable scopes:"},"162":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Scope"},"163":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Grants"},"164":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`sessions:read`"},"165":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-19","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Read sessions, their events and event archives, and webhook delivery ledgers."},"166":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-20","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`sessions:write`"},"167":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-21","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Create sessions, send messages, suspend/resume, redeliver webhooks, reveal the webhook signing secret."},"168":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-22","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`sessions:cancel`"},"169":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-23","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Cancel a session/run."},"170":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-24","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`sessions:delete`"},"171":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-25","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Delete a session and its record."},"172":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-26","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`files:read`"},"173":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-27","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Read captured session files and reusable workspace-file metadata."},"174":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-28","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`files:write` / `files:delete`"},"175":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-29","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Publish and delete reusable workspace-file resources."},"176":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-30","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`assets:write`"},"177":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-31","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Upload content-addressed bytes before publishing a typed workspace resource."},"178":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-32","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`assets:delete`"},"179":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-33","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Delete unreferenced content-addressed bytes."},"180":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-34","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`skills:read` / `skills:write` / `skills:delete`"},"181":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-35","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Administer workspace skills."},"182":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-36","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`tools:read` / `tools:write` / `tools:delete`"},"183":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-37","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Administer workspace custom tools."},"184":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-38","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`instructions:read` / `instructions:write` / `instructions:delete`"},"185":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-39","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Administer workspace instructions."},"186":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-40","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`secrets:read`"},"187":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-41","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"List workspace secrets and read their metadata (never values)."},"188":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-42","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`secrets:write`"},"189":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-43","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Create, rotate, and delete workspace secrets."},"190":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-44","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`mcp:read`"},"191":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-45","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"List and read workspace MCP server configurations."},"192":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-46","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`mcp:write`"},"193":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-47","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Create workspace MCP server configurations."},"194":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-48","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`mcp:delete`"},"195":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-49","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Delete workspace MCP server configurations."},"196":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-50","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`billing:read`"},"197":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-51","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Read billing state and create hosted billing sessions."},"198":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-52","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"`workspaces:delete`"},"199":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-53","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"Owner self-service workspace hard-erase."},"200":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-54","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#scopes","content":"A typical automation token carries `sessions:read`, `sessions:write`, and\r\n`files:read`, plus the resource scopes it publishes. Grant the rest only where the workload needs them — a read-only\r\nreporting token, for example, needs no `sessions:write`."},"201":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-55","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#introspection-whoami","content":"`aex.whoami()` (CLI: `aex whoami`) validates the token and returns the\r\nworkspace id, the token's scopes, and — on current platform deployments — a\r\n`limits` object with the workspace's effective admission caps\r\n(`maxConcurrentSessions`, `submitRatePerMinute`, `spendCapUsd`, `monthSpendUsd`,\r\n`balanceUsd`, `balanceGraceFloorUsd`, `paymentMethodStatus`), resolved by the\r\nsame code the submit gates enforce. Use it as a cheap credential check and to\r\nanticipate `429`/`402` rejections before submitting — see\r\nLimits & quotas and Errors."},"202":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-56","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#rotation-and-revocation","content":"**Rotate** by creating a new token in the dashboard, switching your\r\ndeployment to it, then deleting the old one. Tokens are independent — both\r\nstay valid during the switch, so rotation needs no downtime."},"203":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-57","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#rotation-and-revocation","content":"**Revoke** by deleting the token in the dashboard; deletion takes effect\r\nimmediately (allow up to a minute for in-flight caches to expire)."},"204":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-58","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#rotation-and-revocation","content":"Token create/delete are rate-limited per workspace (see\r\nLimits & quotas)."},"205":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-59","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#rotation-and-revocation","content":"If you cannot reach the dashboard (or suspect workspace-level compromise),\r\ncontact support\\@aex.dev."},"206":{"id":"/docs/guides/authentication-60","page_id":"/docs/guides/authentication","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/authentication#rotation-and-revocation","content":"Provider keys (`apiKeys`) and runtime secrets are a separate, per-call surface —\r\nsee Credentials and Secrets."},"207":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","type":"page","content":"Billing & webhook signing secret","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/billing"},"208":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/billing#billing--webhook-signing-secret","content":"Billing & webhook signing secret"},"209":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/billing#read-the-billing-summary","content":"Read the billing summary"},"210":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/billing#manage-the-subscription","content":"Manage the subscription"},"211":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/billing#read-the-credit-ledger","content":"Read the credit ledger"},"212":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/billing#reveal-the-webhook-signing-secret","content":"Reveal the webhook signing secret"},"213":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#billing--webhook-signing-secret","content":"Workspace-level billing, subscription, and webhook verification calls are\r\ntoken-scoped like every other client call — the workspace is derived\r\nserver-side from the API key."},"214":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#billing--webhook-signing-secret","content":"The billing reads — `aex.billing()`, `aex.billingLedger()`, and the CLI\r\n`aex billing` (and its `ledger&#x60; sub-verb) — require the &#x2A;*`billing:read`**\r\nscope; a token without it fails with `403 insufficient_scope` (see\r\nErrors). This is why the Quickstart mints\r\n`billing:read` alongside `sessions:read` / `sessions:write` / `files:read`."},"215":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#read-the-billing-summary","content":"`aex.billing()` returns the workspace's prepaid balance, current-month spend,\r\nand the spend cap enforced on new sessions, plus plan fields:"},"216":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#read-the-billing-summary","content":"The returned `BillingSummary` is additive-tolerant: fields a newer deployment\r\nreports that this SDK version does not know yet pass through on the object\r\ninstead of being rejected."},"217":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#read-the-billing-summary","content":"CLI equivalent:"},"218":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#manage-the-subscription","content":"`aex.billingCheckout({ planKey })` creates a hosted checkout session for a paid\r\nplan. Open the returned URL in a browser; the workspace plan changes after\r\ncheckout completes and the hosted API confirms the subscription."},"219":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#manage-the-subscription","content":"The optional second argument identifies the mutation and is sent only as the\r\n`Idempotency-Key` header. When omitted, the SDK generates one before transport\r\nretries begin and reuses it for every attempt."},"220":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#manage-the-subscription","content":"`aex.billingPortal()` creates a hosted billing portal session for the workspace:"},"221":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#manage-the-subscription","content":"CLI equivalents:"},"222":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#read-the-credit-ledger","content":"`aex.billingLedger({ limit })` returns recent credit-ledger rows, newest first —\r\nallowance grants, adjustments, and run charges with signed `amountUsd` (credits\r\npositive, charges negative). `limit` is clamped server-side to \\[1, 100] (default\r\n25\\); the read is not cursor-paged."},"223":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#read-the-credit-ledger","content":"CLI equivalent:"},"224":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#reveal-the-webhook-signing-secret","content":"Session webhooks are signed Standard-Webhooks style with a per-workspace secret.\r\n`aex.webhookSigningSecret()` reveals it (creating one on first use) as the\r\n`whsec_<base64>` string that `verifyAexWebhook` takes as `secret`:"},"225":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#reveal-the-webhook-signing-secret","content":"Repeat calls return the SAME value — the hosted API does not rotate the\r\nsigning secret. Treat the reveal as sensitive: store it in your secret manager\r\nand never log it."},"226":{"id":"/docs/guides/billing-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/billing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/billing#reveal-the-webhook-signing-secret","content":"CLI equivalent (prints the bare `whsec_...` string, pipeable into a secret\r\nstore; the reveal never goes to stderr or debug traces):"},"227":{"id":"/docs/guides/cleanup","page_id":"/docs/guides/cleanup","type":"page","content":"Cleanup","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/cleanup"},"228":{"id":"/docs/guides/cleanup-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/cleanup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/cleanup#cleanup","content":"Cleanup"},"229":{"id":"/docs/guides/cleanup-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/cleanup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/cleanup#cleanup","content":"aex owns runtime cleanup after a run ends. This internal work is not a public\r\nsession lifecycle state and is not represented by a synthetic `cleanupStatus`\r\nfield. A terminal RUN event means the run's checkpoint, files, billing, and\r\npublic read model are consistent; explicit session deletion remains a separate\r\noperation."},"230":{"id":"/docs/guides/cleanup-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/cleanup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/cleanup#cleanup","content":"The hosted product uses managed runtimes for all supported providers. Reusable\r\nprovider-session retention is not a supported session option, and the removed\r\nretention field is rejected if supplied."},"231":{"id":"/docs/guides/cleanup-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/cleanup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/cleanup#cleanup","content":"Session sequencing is exposed only through `currentRun` and `lastRun`. Use\r\n`session.delete()` when the session itself should be deleted."},"232":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","type":"page","content":"Credentials","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/credentials"},"233":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/credentials#credentials","content":"Credentials"},"234":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/credentials#the-client-credential","content":"The client credential"},"235":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/credentials#provider-keys","content":"Provider keys"},"236":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/credentials#runtime-secrets","content":"Runtime secrets"},"237":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/credentials#workspace-secrets","content":"Workspace secrets"},"238":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/credentials#networking","content":"Networking"},"239":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/credentials#explicit-call-site-rule","content":"Explicit call-site rule"},"240":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#credentials","content":"aex uses explicit, per-session credentials:"},"241":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#credentials","content":"`AEX_API_KEY` authenticates the SDK or CLI to aex."},"242":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#credentials","content":"`apiKeys` carries BYOK provider keys for the model provider."},"243":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#credentials","content":"`McpServer.remote(..., { headers })` carries MCP auth when a remote MCP server needs it."},"244":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#credentials","content":"`environment.secrets` carries runtime secrets for your own code."},"245":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#credentials","content":"Secrets never belong in reusable session config, files, prompts, or examples."},"246":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#the-client-credential","content":"Pass your aex API key directly to the constructor — `new Aex(apiKey)` — or as\r\nthe `apiKey` option:"},"247":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#the-client-credential","content":"See Authentication for how keys are scoped, rotated, and\r\nissued during the beta."},"248":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#provider-keys","content":"A session selects one upstream provider and must carry a BYOK key for it. Include\r\nadditional provider keys only when subagents may use those providers."},"249":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#provider-keys","content":"Provider keys are used by the managed runtime for model calls. They are not saved\r\nas client defaults."},"250":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#runtime-secrets","content":"Use `environment.secrets` for credentials your code needs at runtime. The value\r\ncan be ephemeral with `Secret.value(...)` or a workspace secret reference with\r\n`Secret.ref(...)`."},"251":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#runtime-secrets","content":"Inside the session, use normal HTTP code for the service:"},"252":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-19","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#workspace-secrets","content":"Store reusable values once, then reference them by name:"},"253":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-20","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#workspace-secrets","content":"Secret reads return metadata only; they never return the stored value."},"254":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-21","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#networking","content":"Networking is open by default within the platform's managed egress ceiling. Use\r\n`environment.networking.mode: \"limited\"` with `allowedHosts` when you want a\r\nsession's own code to reach only named hosts. See Networking for\r\nthe two-layer enforcement model."},"255":{"id":"/docs/guides/credentials-22","page_id":"/docs/guides/credentials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/credentials#explicit-call-site-rule","content":"There is no `defaultSecrets` and no client-held secret state. Each\r\n`aex.sessions.create(...)` or `aex.start(...)` call should show the provider\r\nkeys, MCP auth, and runtime secrets needed for that call."},"256":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","type":"page","content":"Defaults","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/defaults"},"257":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/defaults#defaults","content":"Defaults"},"258":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/defaults#session","content":"Session"},"259":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/defaults#tools-and-mcp","content":"Tools and MCP"},"260":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/defaults#links-and-tickets","content":"Links and tickets"},"261":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/defaults#subagents","content":"Subagents"},"262":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/defaults#workspace","content":"Workspace"},"263":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/defaults#defaults","content":"These are the public values aex applies when you omit the corresponding option.\r\nRuntime-size presets are defined in public\r\n`runtime-sizes.ts`.\r\nFor hard ceilings and adjustable limits, see\r\nLimits & quotas."},"264":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/defaults#session","content":"Option"},"265":{"id":"/docs/guides/defaults-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/defaults#session","content":"Default"},"