ountPath` names a directory, not a destination filename. The attached\r\nfile retains its source/archive filename below that directory; see\r\nFiles."},"551":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas-95","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas#request-scope","content":"Limit"},"552":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas-96","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas#request-scope","content":"Value"},"553":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas-97","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas#request-scope","content":"Adjustable?"},"554":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas-98","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas#request-scope","content":"Signed file URL TTL"},"555":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas-99","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas#request-scope","content":"300 seconds at the API layer"},"556":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas-100","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas#request-scope","content":"Per call with `expiresSeconds`"},"557":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas-101","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas#request-scope","content":"Event-stream connection ticket TTL"},"558":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas-102","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas#request-scope","content":"60 seconds"},"559":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas-103","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits-and-quotas#request-scope","content":"Per mint with `ttlMs`"},"560":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","type":"page","content":"Limits","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/limits"},"561":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/limits#limits","content":"Limits"},"562":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/limits#current-defaults","content":"Current Defaults"},"563":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Product Boundaries"},"564":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/limits#provider-policy-links","content":"Provider Policy Links"},"565":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/limits#unsupported-claims","content":"Unsupported Claims"},"566":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#limits","content":"aex sessions autonomous agents on the hosted managed runtime. The SDK opens durable\r\nsessions, sends turns, streams events, captures files, and exposes auth-gated\r\nreads and downloads."},"567":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#limits","content":"For what the product supports, see Features.\r\nFor the current provider/model set, see the generated\r\nprovider/runtime capability matrix."},"568":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#current-defaults","content":"Area"},"569":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#current-defaults","content":"Default"},"570":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#current-defaults","content":"Workspace storage"},"571":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#current-defaults","content":"500 GB per workspace for captured files and workspace artifacts."},"572":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Area"},"573":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Boundary"},"574":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Runtime"},"575":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"New submissions run on a managed runtime. `runtime.kind` selects `container` (the default), `spot_container`, or `lambda`; `runtime.size` selects a managed machine-size preset (`Sizes.*`). Both fields are optional."},"576":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Provider policy"},"577":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Provider retention, training exclusion, HIPAA/BAA, data residency, abuse policy, and pricing belong to the selected provider account, endpoint, and contract."},"578":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Secrets"},"579":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Provider keys, MCP credentials, and environment secrets are caller-owned. aex excludes secret values from idempotency and uses the explicit secret surfaces described in Secrets."},"580":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-19","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"MCP servers"},"581":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-20","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Remote MCP servers are customer-trusted systems. aex validates declarations and routes credentials; it does not make an untrusted MCP server safe."},"582":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-21","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Files"},"583":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-22","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Captured files, events, and metadata are stored under the session record and downloaded through auth-gated routes. SessionFile content is customer content."},"584":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-23","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Human review"},"585":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-24","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Sessions execute after submission. Cancellation is available, but aex does not pause a session for platform-mediated approval or interactive clarification."},"586":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-25","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Sessions"},"587":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-26","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"The durable product primitive is the session record. Sessions can be resumed by id and auto-suspend after the configured idle window; persistent named agent profiles and saved agent definitions are out of scope."},"588":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-27","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Hosting"},"589":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-28","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"The SDK and CLI connect to the hosted aex API. `baseUrl` may also target the localhost development stack; self-hosting is not supported."},"590":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-29","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"Provider cost"},"591":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-30","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#product-boundaries","content":"BYOK provider-token charges accrue to the selected provider account. Finished results report the cost and provider usage recorded for that run."},"592":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-31","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#provider-policy-links","content":"These links are starting points for provider-owned policy areas; they do not\r\ncreate aex guarantees."},"593":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-32","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#provider-policy-links","content":"Anthropic API data retention policy: https\\://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/api-and-data-retention"},"594":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-33","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#provider-policy-links","content":"OpenAI API data controls: https\\://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/your-data"},"595":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-34","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#provider-policy-links","content":"Mistral privacy and API data handling: https\\://docs.mistral.ai/admin/security-access/privacy"},"596":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-35","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#provider-policy-links","content":"Gemini API data handling: https\\://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/logs-policy"},"597":{"id":"/docs/guides/limits-36","page_id":"/docs/guides/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/limits#unsupported-claims","content":"Do not describe aex as providing self-hosting, provider-wide retention,\r\nHIPAA/BAA or data-residency guarantees, a general-purpose sandbox for every\r\ndownstream service, human-in-the-loop approval checkpoints, or persistent agent\r\nidentity."},"598":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","type":"page","content":"MCP","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mcp"},"599":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"MCP"},"600":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mcp#large-payload-responses","content":"Large-payload responses"},"601":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"MCP support is remote HTTPS/SSE only. Stdio MCP servers are rejected because aex is a remote session dispatcher, not a local process supervisor."},"602":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"Rules:"},"603":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"MCP servers are declared in the session request config (`mcpServers`)."},"604":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"Runtime HITL is disabled."},"605":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"Tool policy must be configured before session start."},"606":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"Enabled MCP tools use `always_allow` provider permissions."},"607":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"`always_ask` is not used by aex MVP."},"608":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"Bearer/OAuth-style auth is carried by the `McpServer` instance (its `headers`); the SDK splits it into the vaulted secrets channel server-side."},"609":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#mcp","content":"Use allowlists for sensitive servers whenever possible."},"610":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#large-payload-responses","content":"aex is a session dispatcher, not an MCP runtime. We intentionally do\r\n**not** interpose on the transport between the model and an upstream MCP\r\nserver, so we cannot elide MCP responses or write them to the session\r\nfilesystem on the user's behalf. Anything an MCP tool returns lands\r\ndirectly in the model's context."},"611":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#large-payload-responses","content":"For ingestion-style MCP servers that return large JSON blobs (search results,\r\ncatalogue dumps, bulk reads), prefer a skill that writes files instead of\r\nputting the whole response in model context:"},"612":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#large-payload-responses","content":"Package the upstream helper as a Skill (`Skill.fromDir` / `Skill.fromUrl`)\nand pass it via the top-level `skills` option. The skill can include a CLI\nbinary or script that the agent invokes with its bash tool."},"613":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#large-payload-responses","content":"Keep any upstream HTTPS credentials in `environment.secrets`."},"614":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#large-payload-responses","content":"Have the CLI write the full payload to the session filesystem. By default,\r\nfiles it creates or modifies are captured automatically; pass\r\n`fileCapture.allowedDirs` only when you want to narrow capture to specific roots.\nReturn only a small handle (path, item count, summary) to the model."},"615":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#large-payload-responses","content":"The agent sees the handle in context; the bytes ride out through\r\n`download()` as normal captured files."},"616":{"id":"/docs/guides/mcp-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mcp#large-payload-responses","content":"If you genuinely want everything in context (small responses, code\r\nsearch, etc.), use MCP. If the payload would blow your context budget,\r\nthe CLI-as-skill pattern is the supported answer — there is no platform\r\nflag to elide MCP responses."},"617":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","type":"page","content":"Networking","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/networking"},"618":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/networking#networking","content":"Networking"},"619":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/networking#paths-that-always-work","content":"Paths that always work"},"620":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/networking#restrict-a-session-to-an-allowlist","content":"Restrict a session to an allowlist"},"621":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/networking#typescript","content":"TypeScript"},"622":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/networking#open-mode","content":"Open mode"},"623":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/networking#ordinary-http-clients-work-without-extra-setup","content":"Ordinary HTTP clients work without extra setup"},"624":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/networking#limitations","content":"Limitations"},"625":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#networking","content":"Session networking is managed by aex. Your code can make ordinary outbound HTTP\r\nrequests, subject to the session's `environment.networking` policy and the\r\nservice-wide safety boundary. Private, loopback, link-local, and otherwise\r\nunsafe destinations remain blocked."},"626":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#networking","content":"`environment.networking` has two modes:"},"627":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#networking","content":"`open` is the default and does not require a per-session allowlist."},"628":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#networking","content":"`limited` restricts supported outbound HTTP clients to the hosts you list in\r\n`allowedHosts`."},"629":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#networking","content":"`allowedHosts` is a useful least-privilege control and an auditable statement of\r\nintent. It is not a security boundary against adversarial code executing inside\r\nthe session; low-level networking that bypasses supported HTTP client behavior\r\nmay fail and remains subject to the service-wide egress policy."},"630":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#paths-that-always-work","content":"These managed capabilities are not subject to `environment.networking`, so you\r\ndo not list their hosts:"},"631":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#paths-that-always-work","content":"The model/provider call for the session and its subagents."},"632":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#paths-that-always-work","content":"The built-in `web_search` and `web_fetch` tools."},"633":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#paths-that-always-work","content":"Remote MCP servers declared in `mcpServers`; see MCP."},"634":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#paths-that-always-work","content":"Package registries used by packages declared in `environment.packages`."},"635":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#paths-that-always-work","content":"`environment.networking` governs other outbound requests made by your code,\r\nsuch as `curl` in the `bash` tool, Python `requests`, Node `fetch`, or a\r\nthird-party SDK."},"636":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#restrict-a-session-to-an-allowlist","content":"Set `mode: \"limited\"` and list the hosts your code needs. A supported HTTP\r\nclient is refused when it requests a host that is neither listed nor covered by\r\none of the managed capabilities above. Package registries implied by\r\n`environment.packages` are allowed automatically."},"637":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-19","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#typescript","content":"`allowedHosts` entries are lowercased host names such as `api.example.com`.\r\nInclude a non-default port when needed (`api.example.com:8443`); a bare host\r\ncovers HTTPS on port 443. Matching is exact, not wildcard or suffix based, so\r\nlist each required host."},"638":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-20","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#typescript","content":"Keep the allowlist in your session options so the network policy stays next to\r\nthe code that needs it."},"639":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-21","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#open-mode","content":"A session that omits `environment.networking` uses `open` mode. Set\r\n`mode: \"open\"` explicitly when you want that choice visible in configuration.\r\nOpen mode removes the per-session allowlist, but the service-wide safety\r\nboundary still applies."},"640":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-22","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#open-mode","content":"Built-in web research uses the managed `web_search` and `web_fetch` tools and\r\ndoes not require an allowlist entry."},"641":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-23","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#ordinary-http-clients-work-without-extra-setup","content":"Use normal HTTP clients without configuring a per-request proxy or installing a\r\ncustom certificate. For example, in a limited session that allows\r\n`api.example.com`:"},"642":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-24","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#ordinary-http-clients-work-without-extra-setup","content":"Clients that override standard network or certificate behavior, or use a\r\nnon-HTTP protocol, may fail even for a listed host. Let the client use its\r\nnormal defaults whenever possible."},"643":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-25","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#limitations","content":"`allowedHosts` applies only in `limited` mode."},"644":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-26","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#limitations","content":"A listed host can still be unavailable under the service-wide safety policy."},"645":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-27","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#limitations","content":"Exact host matching means subdomains must be listed separately."},"646":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-28","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#limitations","content":"Contact support when a required public host is unavailable."},"647":{"id":"/docs/guides/networking-29","page_id":"/docs/guides/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/networking#limitations","content":"For credentialed HTTP calls, pass the credential through\r\n`environment.secrets` and let your code use its normal HTTP client. For remote\r\ntool servers, see MCP. For all session configuration fields, see\r\nSession configuration."},"648":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","type":"page","content":"Quickstart","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/quickstart"},"649":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#quickstart","content":"Quickstart"},"650":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#install","content":"Install"},"651":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#run-a-session","content":"Run a session"},"652":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#reopen-and-continue","content":"Reopen and continue"},"653":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#publish-reusable-inputs","content":"Publish reusable inputs"},"654":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#read-checkpointed-files","content":"Read checkpointed files"},"655":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#one-shot-convenience","content":"One-shot convenience"},"656":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#next","content":"Next"},"657":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#install","content":"Set an aex workspace key and the BYOK key for your model:"},"658":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#install","content":"The workspace key needs `sessions:read`, `sessions:write`, and `files:read` for\r\nthis workflow. Add `billing:read` when the application also reads cost and\r\nbilling-account resources."},"659":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#run-a-session","content":"`finished()` resolves only after `RUN_FINISHED` or `RUN_ERROR`. A\r\n`RUN_FINISHED` result is checkpoint-consistent: its session record, cost,\r\nusage, messages, and files all reflect the same committed run. A `RUN_ERROR`\r\nthat failed before a checkpoint has `files: []` and no `checkpoint`."},"660":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#run-a-session","content":"Held outcomes remain explicit. `suspended` and `awaiting_approval` are not\r\nreported as successful runs, and `result.ok` is true only for `succeeded`."},"661":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#reopen-and-continue","content":"`record.currentRun` describes active work and `record.lastRun` describes the\r\nmost recently completed or held run."},"662":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#publish-reusable-inputs","content":"Workspace resources are versioned and immutable when submitted. Publish local\r\ndrafts first, then pass the returned pinned refs under `assets`:"},"663":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#publish-reusable-inputs","content":"The same pattern applies to `aex.workspace.skills`, `.tools`, and\r\n`.instructions`. Raw uploaded bytes are assets; workspace resources add typed,\r\nversioned meaning to those bytes."},"664":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#read-checkpointed-files","content":"Session file IDs are meaningful only with their checkpoint. File objects carry\r\n`checkpointId`, and ID selectors must include it."},"665":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#one-shot-convenience","content":"`aex.start()` is the one retained convenience for create, send, and finish:"},"666":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#one-shot-convenience","content":"The bundled CLI provides the same one-shot workflow:"},"667":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#next","content":"Composition"},"668":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-19","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#next","content":"Events"},"669":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-20","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#next","content":"Files"},"670":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-21","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#next","content":"Webhooks"},"671":{"id":"/docs/guides/quickstart-22","page_id":"/docs/guides/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/quickstart#next","content":"Provider/runtime capabilities"},"672":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","type":"page","content":"Retries and throttling","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/retries"},"673":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/retries#retries-and-throttling","content":"Retries and throttling"},"674":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/retries#application-runs-are-not-retried","content":"Application runs are not retried"},"675":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/retries#throttling","content":"Throttling"},"676":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#retries-and-throttling","content":"The SDK retries transport failures only when repeating the HTTP request is\r\nprovably safe:"},"677":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#retries-and-throttling","content":"Safe reads (`GET`, `HEAD`, and `OPTIONS`) may retry."},"678":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#retries-and-throttling","content":"A mutation may retry only when it carries a stable `Idempotency-Key`."},"679":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#retries-and-throttling","content":"A `POST`, `PATCH`, `PUT`, or `DELETE` without that key is attempted once."},"680":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#retries-and-throttling","content":"Eligible requests retry network failures and HTTP `429`, `500`, `502`, `503`,\r\n`504`, and `529` with bounded exponential backoff and jitter. `Retry-After` is\r\nhonored. Validation, authentication, not-found, and conflict responses fail\r\nimmediately."},"681":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#retries-and-throttling","content":"Use `retry: false` or `{ maxAttempts: 1 }` for one general transport attempt.\nThe client policy applies both to hosted API requests and to direct\nobject-storage PUTs performed while publishing file, skill, tool, and\ninstruction assets."},"682":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#retries-and-throttling","content":"`session.files.fetch()` is deliberately lower level: it returns the raw\n`Response` from a signed file URL and does not retry that transfer. The bounded\n`session.files.read()` and `session.files.download()` helpers may repeat a safe\nfile GET once only when their per-attempt transfer timeout expires. None of\nthese transfer policies repeat an agent run."},"683":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#application-runs-are-not-retried","content":"The SDK never reruns a whole user scenario after a terminal failure. A failed\r\nrun is the product result a user would observe. Reliability belongs below that\r\nboundary, in idempotent transport, checkpointing, and the hosted runtime."},"684":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#application-runs-are-not-retried","content":"When your application deliberately repeats a create or message mutation, reuse\r\nits idempotency key:"},"685":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#application-runs-are-not-retried","content":"`Aex.start` derives a stable message key from the create key, so repeating the\nsame call cannot create a second billable run. A changed request under the same\nkey fails with an idempotency conflict. Explicit keys may contain at most 255\ncharacters. For a create key short enough to append `:message`, the derived key\nis readable as `<createKey>:message`; longer valid keys use a deterministic\nSHA-256-derived message key that remains within the same limit."},"686":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#application-runs-are-not-retried","content":"For an explicit user-driven retry on an existing session, call\r\n`session.messages.replayLast()` after applying your own policy. It reuses the\r\nlast message key by default."},"687":{"id":"/docs/guides/retries-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/retries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/retries#throttling","content":"After eligible transport attempts are exhausted, the SDK throws\r\n`AexRateLimitError`. Use `isRateLimited(error)` and inspect `status`,\r\n`attempts`, `retryAfterMs`, `source`, and `providerFault`. Error bodies and\r\nsecrets are redacted."},"688":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"page","content":"Secrets","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets"},"689":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#secrets","content":"Secrets"},"690":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#use-a-provider-key-for-one-session","content":"Use A Provider Key For One Session"},"691":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#typescript","content":"TypeScript"},"692":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#cli","content":"CLI"},"693":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#persist-an-env-secret","content":"Persist An Env Secret"},"694":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#set-or-rotate-a-workspace-secret","content":"Set Or Rotate A Workspace Secret"},"695":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#retrieve-secret-metadata","content":"Retrieve Secret Metadata"},"696":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#inject-a-workspace-secret-into-a-session","content":"Inject A Workspace Secret Into A Session"},"697":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#delete-a-workspace-secret","content":"Delete A Workspace Secret"},"698":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/secrets#redaction-scope-and-session-files","content":"Redaction Scope And Session Files"},"699":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#secrets","content":"aex supports BYOK provider keys, per-session credentials, and reusable workspace\r\nsecrets. Secret values are excluded from the idempotency fingerprint and do not\r\nbelong in session config."},"700":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#secrets","content":"Runnable examples need both `AEX_API_KEY` for aex and the matching BYOK\r\nprovider key, such as `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` for Claude."},"701":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#persist-an-env-secret","content":"Create durable secrets through the workspace namespace, then reference the\r\nstored name in later sessions."},"702":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#set-or-rotate-a-workspace-secret","content":"Use `client.workspace.secrets.set(...)` to create a named secret directly. Use\r\n`client.workspace.secrets.rotate(...)` to replace its value while keeping the same name."},"703":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#retrieve-secret-metadata","content":"`list` and `get` return metadata only. They never return the secret value."},"704":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#inject-a-workspace-secret-into-a-session","content":"Reference workspace secrets with `Secret.ref(name)`. The value resolves\r\nserver-side and is injected as the named environment variable."},"705":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#delete-a-workspace-secret","content":"The CLI supports per-session provider and MCP credentials. Workspace secret\r\nadministration is exposed through the SDK."},"706":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#redaction-scope-and-session-files","content":"Registered secret values are redacted from the session's **event stream** (both tool\r\noutput and model-authored surfaces) — a value you inject via `environment.secrets`\r\nis masked regardless of its shape. Two surfaces are intentionally *not* scrubbed:"},"707":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#redaction-scope-and-session-files","content":"**Captured session files** (`session.files.download()` / `.read()` / the `aex download`\r\nzip) are returned **verbatim**. They are your session's own artifacts, so the platform\r\ndoes not rewrite their bytes — if the agent writes a secret into a deliverable file,\r\nthat file contains it. Treat downloaded files as unredacted."},"708":{"id":"/docs/guides/secrets-19","page_id":"/docs/guides/secrets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/secrets#redaction-scope-and-session-files","content":"An **unregistered** secret (a credential the session produces itself and never declared\r\nvia `environment.secrets`) can only be masked heuristically by shape; register the\r\nvalues you care about so they are masked by value."},"709":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","type":"page","content":"Session configuration","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/session-config"},"710":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"Session configuration"},"711":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/session-config#cli","content":"CLI"},"712":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`aex.sessions.create(...)` accepts the durable session configuration. The\r\none-shot `aex.start(...)` accepts the same fields plus `message`,\r\n`messageIdempotencyKey`, `deleteAfter`, and stream options."},"713":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"Core fields include:"},"714":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`model` and optional `provider`"},"715":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`system`"},"716":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"immutable workspace refs grouped under `assets`"},"717":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`builtinTools`"},"718":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`mcpServers`"},"719":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`environment`"},"720":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`fileCapture`"},"721":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`runtime`, `metadata`, and `overrides`"},"722":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`outputMode`, `responseFormat`, `approvalGate`, and `webhook`"},"723":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`apiKeys` and `idempotencyKey`"},"724":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"Secrets are never part of a reusable JSON config. Supply provider credentials\r\nthrough `apiKeys` and runtime secrets through `environment.secrets` at the call\r\nsite."},"725":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#session-configuration","content":"`assets` accepts only refs returned by `aex.workspace.files`, `skills`, `tools`,\r\nand `instructions`. Publish local drafts before create; there is no implicit\r\nupload or compatibility field."},"726":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-config-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-config#cli","content":"`aex start` accepts a credential-free JSON config through `--config`, or\r\nexplicit flags such as `--model`, `--system`, `--prompt`, `--mcp`,\r\n`--runtime-size`, and `--session-timeout`. Reusable resources are published and\r\nattached with repeatable `--skill`, `--tool`, `--instructions`, and `--file`\r\nflags. The legacy instruction flag is not accepted."},"727":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","type":"page","content":"Session archives","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/session-record"},"728":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/session-record#session-archives","content":"Session archives"},"729":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/session-record#listing-sessions","content":"Listing sessions"},"730":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"Downloading a session archive"},"731":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#session-archives","content":"`Session` is the one live state model returned by `aex.sessions.get(...)`,\r\n`session.refresh()`, and finished run results. A session archive is the\r\npublic-safe downloadable bundle of that state, typed events, captured files,\r\nand versioned manifest metadata."},"732":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#listing-sessions","content":"`aex.sessions.list(query?)` enumerates the sessions in this workspace, most-recent first, one page at a time. The workspace is derived server-side from the API key, so this only ever returns your own sessions. It is the workspace-wide discovery entry point: open a row with `aex.sessions.open(id)`, then use `session.files.list()` / `.read(...)` (see Files) to reach that session's deliverables."},"733":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#listing-sessions","content":"`query` fields are all optional: `status` (single session lifecycle status, e.g. `\"idle\"`), `since` (ISO-8601 lower bound on `createdAt`), `limit` (an integer from 1 through 100; default 25), and `cursor` (the opaque keyset cursor from a prior page's `nextCursor`, absent on the last page). Invalid values fail before the request. Each page row is a public-safe `SessionSummary` (`id`, `status`, `runtime`, `acceptsMessages`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `costUsd` once a RUN terminal is committed); it deliberately omits the submission snapshot (model / system / env). Use `aex.sessions.get(id)` or `session.record` for the canonical session read, and the `messages`, `events`, and `files` namespaces for authoritative run data."},"734":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`session.download()` and `aex download <session-id>` return a zip with this layout:"},"735":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`manifest.json` is versioned as `SessionRecordManifestV1`:"},"736":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"Field"},"737":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"Meaning"},"738":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`schemaVersion`"},"739":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`aex.session-record.manifest.v1`."},"740":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`sessionRecordSchemaVersion`"},"741":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`aex.session-record.v1`."},"742":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`sessionId`"},"743":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"The session the archive was assembled for."},"744":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`namespaces[]`"},"745":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"The documented top-level namespaces: `metadata`, `events`, `files`."},"746":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`files[]`"},"747":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-19","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"Inventory of expected and present files with `namespace`, `path`, `role`, and `status`."},"748":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-20","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`sessionFiles[]`"},"749":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-21","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"Session file metadata for entries present under the `files/` namespace."},"750":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-22","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`errors[]`"},"751":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-23","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"Per-artifact byte fetch failures during archive assembly."},"752":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-24","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"Current v1 downloads always include `metadata/session.json` and `events/events.jsonl`. `events/events.jsonl` contains typed event-channel records only; internal diagnostics and full internal streams are not mixed into that file."},"753":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-25","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"`metadata/submission.json` is present only when the session read shape includes a public-safe submission snapshot. `metadata/cost.json` is present only when the session read shape includes public `costTelemetry`; otherwise cost stays `pending`. `metadata/custody.json` remains `pending` until the custody manifest writer and public read surface land. `events/manifest.json` remains `unavailable` in this client-side slice because there is no public coordinator-manifest download route."},"754":{"id":"/docs/guides/session-record-26","page_id":"/docs/guides/session-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/session-record#downloading-a-session-archive","content":"The record boundary is public-safe. It must not contain provider API keys, runner bearers, workspace tokens, signed URLs, raw provider response bodies, object-store keys, Vault ids, raw query strings, secret-shaped values, or internal diagnostic files. Credentials are supplied per session and vaulted separately for the session lifetime."},"755":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","type":"page","content":"Skills","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/skills"},"756":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/skills#skills","content":"Skills"},"757":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/skills#immutable-versions","content":"Immutable versions"},"758":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/skills#workspace-administration","content":"Workspace administration"},"759":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#skills","content":"A skill is a `SKILL.md` bundle plus optional supporting files. Build a local\r\ndraft with a `Skill.from*` factory, publish it to the workspace, and attach the\r\nreturned immutable ref under `assets.skills`."},"760":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#skills","content":"Available draft factories:"},"761":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#skills","content":"`Skill.fromDir(path, { name? })`"},"762":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#skills","content":"`Skill.fromUrl(url, { name?, sha256?, timeoutMs?, fetch? })`"},"763":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#skills","content":"`Skill.fromFiles({ name?, files, meta? })`"},"764":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#skills","content":"`Skill.fromContent(skillMd, { name? })`"},"765":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#skills","content":"`Skill.fromBytes({ name?, zip })`"},"766":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#skills","content":"Every bundle needs a root `SKILL.md` with a non-empty `description` in YAML\r\nfrontmatter. Names are validated locally, and archives are canonicalized and\r\ncontent-hashed before publication."},"767":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#immutable-versions","content":"Publication returns a `WorkspaceSkillRecord` containing a stable `resourceId`,\r\nan immutable `version`, and the exact `assetId`/`contentHash`. Publishing new\r\nbytes creates another version. Existing session submissions remain pinned to\r\ntheir recorded version; they cannot silently observe later edits."},"768":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#immutable-versions","content":"Drafts cannot be submitted or serialized directly. This keeps the only\r\npromotion path visible and auditable:"},"769":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#workspace-administration","content":"List calls return `{ resources, nextCursor? }`. `limit` defaults to 100 and\r\nmust be an integer from 1 through 100."},"770":{"id":"/docs/guides/skills-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/skills#workspace-administration","content":"Skills are distinct from custom tools. The runtime exposes skills through its\r\nskill-loading capability; executable custom functions belong in\r\n`assets.tools`."},"771":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","type":"page","content":"Call a vision API from a skill","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills"},"772":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#call-a-vision-api-from-a-skill","content":"Call a vision API from a skill"},"773":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#submit-the-session","content":"Submit the session"},"774":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#call-the-provider-from-the-skill","content":"Call the provider from the skill"},"775":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#payload-size","content":"Payload size"},"776":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#call-a-vision-api-from-a-skill","content":"aex has no built-in vision tool. The agent's `provider` / `model` selects the\r\nreasoning model for the session; if a skill needs image understanding mid-session, ship a\r\nskill that calls the vision provider with normal HTTP and pass that provider key\r\nas a runtime secret."},"777":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#call-a-vision-api-from-a-skill","content":"The runnable example lives at `vision-skill/` in aexhq/examples.\r\nIt captions a frame with ByteDance Doubao Seed Vision (Ark) and returns a\r\nper-noun \"does the frame depict X?\" verdict."},"778":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#submit-the-session","content":"`Skill.fromDir(\"./vision-skill\", ...)` is resolved relative to the process\r\nCWD. Run the script from the directory that contains `vision-skill/` (the\r\nroot of the examples repo)."},"779":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#call-the-provider-from-the-skill","content":"Inside the session, the skill reads `DOUBAO_API_KEY` and makes an\r\nOpenAI-compatible chat-completions request with Python's standard HTTP client.\r\nThe image is base64-inlined as a data URL in the request body:"},"780":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#call-the-provider-from-the-skill","content":"The same pattern works for OpenAI, Gemini's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, or any\r\nother HTTPS model API. Put the key in `environment.secrets`, allow-list the host\r\nwhen using limited networking, and use the provider's normal SDK or HTTP API."},"781":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#payload-size","content":"Base64 images are larger than their source files. Scale frames before captioning\r\nwhen possible, for example:"},"782":{"id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/vision-skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/vision-skills#payload-size","content":"This keeps upload size and model cost bounded without losing the signal most\r\nvision models need."},"783":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","type":"page","content":"Webhooks","breadcrumbs":["aex","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/webhooks"},"784":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#webhooks","content":"Webhooks"},"785":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#register-a-callback","content":"Register a callback"},"786":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#what-gets-delivered","content":"What gets delivered"},"787":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#verify-deliveries","content":"Verify deliveries"},"788":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#delivery-ledger-and-redelivery","content":"Delivery ledger and redelivery"},"789":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#webhooks","content":"aex can notify your endpoint whenever a run finishes. Register the callback on a\r\nsession and the platform delivers one run-scoped event after each run finalizes:\r\n`run.finished` for AG-UI `RUN_FINISHED`, or `run.error` for `RUN_ERROR`. Sending\r\nanother message on the same session produces another independently identifiable\r\ndelivery."},"790":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#register-a-callback","content":"The URL must be `https`. The callback URL is an operational concern, not part\r\nof the submission fingerprint: retrying the same submission with the same\r\nidempotency key but a different callback URL never conflicts."},"791":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#what-gets-delivered","content":"Each finalized run produces one frozen CloudEvents envelope. A successful\r\n`run.finished` delivery is sent only after its checkpoint and session-file\r\nrevision are committed and the session read model is consistent. A `run.error`\r\ndelivery represents the corresponding finalized `RUN_ERROR`; `checkpoint` is\r\npresent only when that run committed one. Retries and manual redelivery resend\r\nthe same bytes and `webhook-id`."},"792":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#what-gets-delivered","content":"`subject` and `data.runId` identify the run; `data.sessionId` identifies the\r\nresumable thread. `outcome` is the terminal run outcome. `reason` and\r\n`failureClass` carry failure detail for `run.error`; `checkpoint` and\r\n`costTelemetry` are included when available."},"793":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#verify-deliveries","content":"Deliveries are signed Standard Webhooks\r\nstyle: HMAC-SHA256 over `` `${webhook-id}.${webhook-timestamp}.${rawBody}` ``,\r\nsent in three headers — `webhook-id` (stable for that run across retries; your dedupe key),\r\n`webhook-timestamp` (unix seconds), and `webhook-signature` (a space-delimited\r\nlist of `v1,<base64>` entries)."},"794":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#verify-deliveries","content":"The signing key is a per-workspace secret. Reveal it (it is created on first\r\nuse) with either surface:"},"795":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#verify-deliveries","content":"Verify inbound requests with the exported `verifyAexWebhook` — pure Web Crypto,\r\nidentical under Bun and Node, and interoperable with the `standardwebhooks`\r\nreference library:"},"796":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#verify-deliveries","content":"`verifyAexWebhook` rejects stale timestamps (default tolerance 300 seconds) and\r\ncompares signatures constant-time. It accepts every `v1` entry in the signature\r\nlist, so it is already rotation-ready — but **server-side rotation of the\r\nsigning secret is not available yet**: `aex webhooks secret` reveals or creates\r\nthe one workspace secret and there is no rotate endpoint today. If your secret\r\nis compromised, contact support\\@aex.dev."},"797":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#delivery-ledger-and-redelivery","content":"Each session keeps a ledger with one row per finalized run, including its\r\n`runId`, `turnSeq`, event type, attempts, last status code, and last error:"},"798":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#delivery-ledger-and-redelivery","content":"Redelivery re-sends that run's frozen payload with the **same** `webhook-id`, so\r\na consumer that dedupes on `webhook-id` handles retries, redeliveries, and\r\nat-least-once delivery uniformly. Different runs have different delivery IDs.\r\nAn empty ledger means the session carried no `webhook` or no run has finalized\r\nyet."},"799":{"id":"/docs/guides/webhooks-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/webhooks#delivery-ledger-and-redelivery","content":"For the terminal-event mechanics behind delivery timing, see\r\nEvents."},"800":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli","type":"page","content":"CLI","breadcrumbs":["aex","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/cli"},"801":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ref