},"1180":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-226","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#aexnotfounderror","content":"404 — the requested resource was not found."},"1181":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-227","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#aexnotfounderror","content":"Members:"},"1182":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-228","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#aexnotfounderror","content":"`constructor` (Constructor)"},"1183":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-229","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#aexratelimiterror","content":"Structured throttle error. Extends the contracts AexRateLimitErrorBase\r\n(the SINGLE rate-limit class the wire→exception factory also throws, so\r\n`isRateLimited` recognises BOTH — no split-brain) and enriches it with the\r\nretry-layer detail: `attempts`, `source`, and an upstream `providerFault`.\r\n`retryAfterMs` is inherited. The `message` is a fixed, non-leaky summary — it\r\nnever echoes the raw error body (which is still available, redacted, on `.body`)."},"1184":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-230","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#aexratelimiterror","content":"Members:"},"1185":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-231","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#aexratelimiterror","content":"`constructor` (Constructor)"},"1186":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-232","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#aexratelimiterror","content":"`attempts` (Property)"},"1187":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-233","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#aexratelimiterror","content":"`providerFault` (Property)"},"1188":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-234","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#aexratelimiterror","content":"`source` (Property)"},"1189":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-235","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#cleanuperror","content":"Members:"},"1190":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-236","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#cleanuperror","content":"`constructor` (Constructor)"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-237","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#credentialvalidationerror","content":"Members:"},"1192":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-238","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#credentialvalidationerror","content":"`constructor` (Constructor)"},"1193":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-239","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"File — arbitrary bytes (single file or zipped folder) delivered to\r\nthe agent as a mounted runtime resource. The managed runtime UNZIPS the\r\nsnapshotted bytes into the `mountPath` DIRECTORY during workspace\r\nmaterialization, preserving the real filename + extension."},"1194":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-240","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"const settings = await File.fromPath(\"./settings.json\");\r\nconst dataset = await File.fromPath(\"./data/\");\r\nconst input = await client.workspace.files.publish(settings);\r\nawait client.start(\\{ assets: \\{ files: \\[input] }, message: \"...\" });"},"1195":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-241","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"`mountPath` is the absolute container directory the file unzips into; it\r\ndefaults to `/workspace` (the agent's default working directory), so a file\r\nhanded with no `mountPath` lands directly in the agent's cwd — a single file\r\n`subtitles.srt` becomes `/workspace/subtitles.srt`, a folder lands its entries\r\nunder `/workspace/`. The resolved path is surfaced back on the Session record."},"1196":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-242","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"FIDELITY: a directory walk captures executable bits and symlinks into a\r\n`.aexmeta.json` sidecar (emitted only when such metadata exists, so a\r\npure-content bundle stays byte-identical → dedup continuity), and honors\r\n`.aexignore` (gitignore-compatible) plus always-on defaults (`.git/`,\r\n`node_modules/`). SCALE: a large input (total raw size over the streaming\r\nthreshold, `File.fromPath` only) is uploaded via a streaming two-pass\r\nmultipart flow that holds only one entry + one part in memory within the\nruntime asset archive envelope."},"1197":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-243","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"Publish drafts through `aex.workspace.files.publish(file)`, then pin the\r\nreturned immutable ref in `assets.files`."},"1198":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-244","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"Members:"},"1199":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-245","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"`isDraft` (Accessor)"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-246","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"`ref` (Accessor)"},"1201":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-247","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"`toJSON` (Method)"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-248","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"`fromBytes` (Method)"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/reference/sdk-249","page_id":"/docs/reference/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/sdk#file","content":"`fromPath` (Method)"},"1204":{"id