ist, but the service-wide safety\r\nboundary still applies."],[759,"A skill is a `SKILL.md` bundle plus optional supporting files. Build a local\r\ndraft with a `Skill.from*` factory, publish it to the workspace, and attach the\r\nreturned immutable ref under `assets.skills`."],[1257,"A Skill is a draft workspace bundle of instructional /\r\nexecutable content (`SKILL.md` at the bundle root plus any supporting files).\r\nIt is distinct from a Tool: a session gets a single `skills` meta-tool\r\n(list/load) rather than one load-tool per skill."],[451,"A string ID alone is intentionally rejected because an ID without a revision\ncan resolve inconsistently after a later run."],[1424,"A structured, redaction-safe description of an UPSTREAM provider fault the aex\r\nruntime surfaces on a failed turn (a rate limit, an overloaded provider, a\r\nquota exhaustion, or a generic provider error). It is a sibling of the\r\nAPI-plane throttle: the container/runtime emits this shape on the terminal\r\nerror and the SDK re-exposes it on AexRateLimitError.providerFault so\r\ncallers get one place to read \"the model provider throttled us\"."],[1383,"A subagent child session, enumerated under its parent via `GET /api/sessions/:id/children`.\nThis is a read-only lineage snapshot. Its `id` addresses the child's events,\ncheckpointed files, and descendants, but not the top-level session get/control\nroutes."],[161,"A token carries a set of **scopes**; every API route requires one, and a token\r\nthat lacks the route's scope fails with `403 insufficient_scope` naming the\r\nmissing scope. The customer-grantable scopes:"],[200,"A typical automation token carries `sessions:read`, `sessions:write`, and\r\n`files:read`, plus the resource scopes it publishes. Grant the rest only where the workload needs them — a read-only\r\nreporting token, for example, needs no `sessions:write`."],[391,"A workspace deletion fence won the admission race, so the workspace no longer accepts new session work. The body carries `workspaceStatus` (normally `deleting`). Use an active workspace."],[1919,"absolute paths (`/foo`, `C:\\foo`, `\\\\server\\share`)"],[80,"Access"],[1627,"Accessor over the session's assistant messages. `session.messages` returns\r\nthis synchronously; each method fetches on call."],[1574,"Accessor over the session's captured files (`session.files`):\r\nenumerate, read one as capped text, locate/resolve, and download."],[1536,"Accessor over the session's events. Snapshot/polling reads yield durable\r\nAexEventViews with a replay cursor. The live coordinator may also\r\nyield provisional AexStreamEventViews with `replayable:false` and a\r\nper-run `liveSequence` instead of a durable `sequence`."],[1774,"Accessor over the session's run-scoped webhook ledger (`session.webhooks`)."],[13,"Added a clearer reference entry point for SDK, CLI, events, and provider/runtime capabilities."],[11,"Added automatic immutable canary publication and evidence-backed npm\r\npromotion."],[9,"Added checkpoint-aware session file access and memory-bounded event iterators."],[12,"Added top-level examples, integrations, support, and changelog pages."],[468,"Adjustable?"],[500,"Adjustable?"],[537,"Adjustable?"],[553,"Adjustable?"],[183,"Administer workspace custom tools."],[185,"Administer workspace instructions."],[181,"Administer workspace skills."],[45,"aex"],[789,"aex can notify your endpoint whenever a run finishes. Register the callback on a\r\nsession and the platform delivers one run-scoped event after each run finalizes:\r\n`run.finished` for AG-UI `RUN_FINISHED`, or `run.error` for `RUN_ERROR`. Sending\r\nanother message on the same session produces another independently identifiable\r\ndelivery."],[110,"aex exposes one submission shape across supported providers:"],[776,"aex has no built-in vision tool. The agent's `provider` / `model` selects the\r\nreasoning model for the session; if a skill needs image understanding mid-session, ship a\r\nskill that calls the vision provider with normal HTTP and pass that provider key\r\nas a runtime secret."],[610,"aex is a session dispatcher, not an MCP runtime. We intentionally do\r\n**not** interpose on the transport between the model and an upstream MCP\r\nserver, so we cannot elide MCP responses or write them to the session\r\nfilesystem on the user's behalf. Anything an MCP tool returns lands\r\ndirectly in the model's context."],[35,"aex is an agent execution platform for launching autonomous agents from a simple TypeScript SDK and CLI."],[44,"aex is an agent execution platform for launching autonomous agents from a simple TypeScript SDK and CLI."],[51,"aex is an agent execution platform for launching autonomous agents from a simple TypeScript SDK and CLI."],[154,"aex is currently in **invite-only beta**. Workspaces and their initial API\r\ntokens are provisioned by the aex team — contact support\\@aex.dev for beta\r\naccess. Once your workspace exists, you can create and delete additional tokens\r\nin the dashboard at https\\://aex.dev."],[70,"aex keeps integrations explicit in the SDK call site so sessions are reproducible and auditable."],[229,"aex owns runtime cleanup after a run ends. This internal work is not a public\r\nsession lifecycle state and is not represented by a synthetic `cleanupStatus`\r\nfield. A terminal RUN event means the run's checkpoint, files, billing, and\r\npublic read model are consistent; explicit session deletion remains a separate\r\noperation."],[566,"aex sessions autonomous agents on the hosted managed runtime. The SDK opens durable\r\nsessions, sends turns, streams events, captures files, and exposes auth-gated\r\nreads and downloads."],[1826,"aex signs every delivery HMAC-SHA256 over `${webhook-id}.${webhook-timestamp}.${rawBody}`\nand sends three headers:"],[699,"aex supports BYOK provider keys, per-session credentials, and reusable workspace\r\nsecrets. Secret values are excluded from the idempotency fingerprint and do not\r\nbelong in session config."],[240,"aex uses explicit, per-session credentials:"],[687,"After eligible transport attempts are exhausted, the SDK throws\r\n`AexRateLimitError`. Use `isRateLimited(error)` and inspect `status`,\r\n`attempts`, `retryAfterMs`, `source`, and `providerFault`. Error bodies and\r\nsecrets are redacted."],[31,"Agent composition"],[484,"Agent iterations"],[29,"Agent runtime"],[86,"Agent tools"],[856,"All new submissions run on the managed runtime. Public support is expressed as supported providers and supported model ids."],[1995,"All preset tokens, ordered as declared. Handy for CLI help + validation."],[127,"All submissions run on a managed runtime. The optional `runtime` object has two\r\nindependent selectors:"],[1941,"All upstream providers that can serve a model id, in declaration order.\nReturns `[]` for an unknown model."],[708,"An **unregistered** secret (a credential the session produces itself and never declared\r\nvia `environment.secrets`) can only be masked heuristically by shape; register the\r\nvalues you care about so they are masked by value."],[158,"An aex API key is **self-describing**: it embeds the plane (`dev` / `prd`) and\r\nregion it was minted for. The constructor parses the key and routes accordingly,\r\nwith **zero network**:"],[516,"An archive that exceeds any of these bounds is rejected before its contents are\r\navailable to session code; a partial archive is never exposed."],[91,"An array such as `[BuiltinTools.bash, BuiltinTools.read_file]` selects an\r\nexplicit subset."],[113,"Anthropic"],[846,"Anthropic"],[862,"Anthropic"],[593,"Anthropic API data retention policy: https\\://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/api-and-data-retention"],[40,"Anthropic, DeepSeek, OpenAI, Gemini, Mistral, OpenRouter, and Doubao behind one submission shape."],[674,"Application runs are not retried"],[414,"Archives"],[568,"Area"],[572,"Area"],[447,"As a run boots, each attached input archive is checked against a separate\nruntime materialization en